GENERAL JUTSU REFERENCE — KONOHAGAKURE ACADEMY DIGEST
Foundational techniques for the aspiring shinobi

The three basic jutsu categories:
- Ninjutsu: chakra-molded techniques, often nature-based.
- Genjutsu: illusions cast on a target's chakra system.
- Taijutsu: hand-to-hand combat and body techniques.

Academy Graduation Three (E-rank):
- Transformation Technique (Henge): assume another's appearance.
- Clone Technique (Bunshin): create insubstantial illusory copies.
- Substitution Technique (Kawarimi): swap places with a nearby object
  to evade an attack.

Common Field Techniques:
- Body Flicker (Shunshin): high-speed short-range movement.
- Rope Escape, Wall/Tree Climbing (chakra control basics).
- Shadow Clone Technique (forbidden-tier, Jonin discretion).

Every shinobi builds from these foundations. Master chakra control
first; power without control is a danger to oneself and one's comrades.
